; Test whether an object is held by the subject
;
; Tests the chain of holders of an object: is it carried by the subject
; (#R$B6EA: 0 is the player), directly or inside something the subject
; carries. $9C78 takes the object from the first object slot (#R$B6E8); $9C7B
; takes the id in A. The id $FF (no object) counts as held. Objects lying at a
; location (holder $FF) are not held.
; .
; Part of the walk is #R$9C8A.
;
; A Object id ($9C7B only; $9C78 loads it from $B6E8)
; O:F Carry set when the object is held by the subject, or A was $FF; carry clear when not
; O:HL $B6EA, the address of the subject id
@label=CheckObject1Held
c$9C78 LD A,($B6E8)
@label=CheckHeldBySubject
*$9C7B LD HL,$B6EA
 $9C7E CP $FF           ; no object: counts as held
 $9C80 SCF
 $9C81 RET Z
 $9C82 PUSH IX          ; IX is not preserved by #R$9C8A
 $9C84 CALL $9C8A       
 $9C87 POP IX
 $9C89 RET
